# Backend conventions

## General
- All text/JSON I/O uses `encoding="utf-8"` (Windows defaults to cp1252). Config is read with `utf-8-sig` to tolerate BOMs.
- Writes that must not corrupt (session.json, tracker) go to a temp file, then `os.replace`.
- Import heavy SDKs lazily inside the client (`anthropic` is imported in `ClaudeClient.__init__`).
- Never read or print `.env`; get keys via `config.api_key(name)`.

## Jev (`backend/jev/`)
- Official endpoint only: `POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone`, model pinned `jev-1.13.0`. Log the response `model`.
- `state` is sent as `{"posting": text}`; truncated to ~30k tokens (Jev caps state + longest question at 32k).
- Every noul has `criteria.true` / `criteria.false`. Phrase so high = yes; never ask negated duplicates.
- Jev is weak at dates, counting and math: use it to decide existence/category, and keep arithmetic in code.
- New question -> add to `QUESTIONS` and, if it maps to Excel, to `EXISTENCE` / `CHOICE_COLUMNS`; then update `derive.py`.

## Claude Haiku 5.5 (`backend/llm/`)
- Model `claude-haiku-5-5`, Messages API, schema in `output_config.format` (`type: json_schema`), `output_config.effort = "low"`.
- Do NOT send `temperature`, `top_p` or `top_k` (400 on this model).
- Structured outputs reject `maxItems` (only `minItems` 0/1). Put caps in the description and enforce in code (see `MAX_ROLE_CATEGORIES`).
- Every schema property is required + nullable; `additionalProperties: false`. Fields are ordered like Excel columns.
- Pricing jumps 5x above 100k input tokens; `token_warn` (80k) guards it.

## Excel (`backend/excel/tracker.py`)
- Locate columns by header name in table `Applications`, never by letter.
- Default is fill-only-empty; overwriting requires `force_columns`.
- Dates are written as `datetime` with `yyyy-mm-dd` format. New rows get the Days_Since_Applied structured-reference formula and a relative `Folder` hyperlink.
- Call `check_writable()` before creating anything on disk, so a locked tracker leaves no orphan folder.
- openpyxl drops charts/images on save; the tracker has neither. Re-verify if that changes.
